<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jamaica Labour Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1943–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as JLP</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a> Labour Party is one of Jamaica's two main political parties, founded in 1943 by the trade unionist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-bustamante">Alexander Bustamante</a>, who led it to victory in the first elections under universal suffrage in 1944. Bustamante became the country's first prime minister at independence in 1962. Generally conservative and pro-business, the party has alternated in power with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-national-party">People's National Party</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jamaica-labour-party.jpg" alt="Jamaica Labour Party" width="320" height="119" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Jamaica Labour Party (Original author of the graphic currently unknown.) · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jamaica_Labour_Party_Logo_(2024-present).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
